.TH pdfpagecount 1 "05 November 2026"
.SH NAME
pdfpagecount \- count the pages of a PDF by walking its page tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfpagecount
[options]
.RI [ PDF-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfpagecount
opens a PDF the way the other Poppler utilities do (repairing a damaged
xref table and trying an empty user password), walks the page tree from the
catalog's /Pages root and prints the number of leaf page objects it reaches.
.PP
The count comes only from document structure. The root /Count entry, the
linearization dictionary, the Info dictionary, XMP metadata and page content
are never used, so a document cannot claim its own page count.
.PP
Kids are classified the way Poppler builds its page list: a kid that is
/Type /Page, or a dictionary without /Kids, is a page; any other dictionary
is an intermediate node; a kid that does not resolve to a dictionary is
skipped. A page referenced from several places counts every time it is
referenced, because Poppler renders it every time.
.PP
On success the only output is one decimal integer, at least 1, followed by a
newline. Diagnostics go to standard error, are fixed strings and never include
document data; Poppler's own messages are suppressed.
.PP
Run it under a memory limit and a timeout, and pass
.B "\-f 1 \-l"
.I N
with the count to the other utilities: they clamp
.B \-l
to the claimed page count, so the count bounds their work but they may still
process fewer pages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-max\-pages " number"
Fail with exit code 3 if the tree holds more than
.I number
pages (default 100000, at most 1000000000). Kid entries examined, including
ones that count nothing, are capped at twice this plus 64.
.TP
.BI \-max\-depth " number"
Fail with exit code 3 if the tree is more than
.I number
levels deep (default 256).
.TP
.B \-claimed
Also print the root /Count entry on a second line, or "none" if it is not
an integer. For diagnostics only; never use it as the page count.
.TP
.B \-v
Print copyright and version information.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage information.
.RB ( \-help
and
.B \-\-help
are equivalent.) Every long option also accepts a leading double dash.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
0
The page count was printed.
.TP
1
The file could not be opened or is not a repairable PDF, or the output
could not be written.
.TP
2
The file is encrypted and needs a password (or uses an unknown security
handler).
.TP
3
The page count, tree depth or work budget exceeds its limit, or memory ran
out.
.TP
4
The page tree is malformed: no valid /Pages root, no pages, a kid that is not
an indirect reference, a /Kids entry that is not an array, a page Poppler
rejects, a cycle, or a root without /Kids that is not a lone page.
.TP
99
Invalid command line.
.PP
On any failure nothing is printed on stdout.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdfinfo (1),
.BR pdftotext (1),
.BR pdftoppm (1)
